Subject: [PATCH] Add a hybrid nav: More tab + Wishlist screen (website parity,
 Option C)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The website's header has more links than the app's 3-tab bottom bar
covers (Categories, Live Classes, My Learning, Messages, Purchases,
Business, Instructor Studio, plus search/wishlist/cart). Mocked up
three ways to close that gap; the chosen approach keeps the existing
bottom tabs and adds what's missing rather than rebuilding navigation
from scratch:

- Destinations/BottomNavBar: a 4th "More" tab alongside Explore/My
  Learning/Account.
- New MoreScreen: a 5-row list for Live Classes, Messages, Purchases,
  EduQuinn Business, and Instructor Studio — none of these have native
  screens (by original scope), so each row hands off to the real
  website page via Chrome Custom Tabs, the same pattern already used
  for the Catalog screen's promo cards and the Paynow checkout flow.
- New WishlistScreen/WishlistViewModel: the Catalog top bar gets a
  wishlist icon (next to the existing cart icon) with a badge count,
  opening a screen built from the existing WishlistRepository and the
  already-redesigned CourseCard component unchanged.
- Bump versionCode/versionName for the next Play Console upload.

Categories already live on the Catalog screen (pills) and My Learning
already has its own tab, so More only needed the remaining 5 links. A
top-bar search icon was left out deliberately — the Catalog hero's
search field already covers it on the one screen that has one.

